WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.262
Unit 1 is the guide's Step 9.

2
00:00:02.262 --> 00:00:06.790
Gather the security definitions from
Steps 3 to 8 into one initiative,

3
00:00:06.790 --> 00:00:12.253
assigned at the intermediate root: DDoS
protection on virtual networks and its logs,

4
00:00:12.253 --> 00:00:16.546
the firewall-enabled and firewall-mode
policies that Learn's page,

5
00:00:16.546 --> 00:00:20.448
Azure Web Application Firewall
and Azure Policy, describes,

6
00:00:20.448 --> 00:00:24.975
the private D N S and public-access
policies, and the Key Vault policies.

7
00:00:24.975 --> 00:00:27.320
Built-in definitions differ by cloud,

8
00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:30.725
so look each one up by display
name in the cloud you're in.

9
00:00:30.725 --> 00:00:33.962
Assign the initiative in
do-not-enforce mode first.

10
00:00:33.962 --> 00:00:39.151
Policies with deploy-if-not-exists or modify
effects need a managed identity and a

11
00:00:39.151 --> 00:00:42.509
role; grant the narrowest
role each definition names,

12
00:00:42.509 --> 00:00:45.562
not Contributor, where
the initiative allows it.

13
00:00:45.562 --> 00:00:48.822
After at least one evaluation
cycle and a review of

14
00:00:48.822 --> 00:00:52.237
the non-compliant list with
owners, switch to Default.

15
00:00:52.237 --> 00:00:56.236
Then run a remediation task
for each deploy-if-not-exists

16
00:00:56.236 --> 00:00:59.350
or modify policy, to
fix what already exists.
